==English==

===Etymology===
Latinate variant of {{m|en|Lucy}}, or today borrowed from modern Italian. Name of a Sicilian martyr, {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|Lucia}}, feminine form of the Roman [[praenomen]] {{m|la|Lucius}}.

